Jesse Luehrs <jlueh...@uiuc.edu> wrote:

> Finally, if you take away the unlimited items

There are no such thing. Pudding farming, and all
its rewards, are limited entirely by player
patience, and the usual real objection of those
determined to remove pudding farming from the game
is that they, lacking sufficient patience, are at a
score table disadvantage to patience players while
NetHack supports any form of patience game play.

> and the unlimited score,

The unlimited score is also a red herring, the score
counter rolls, so the score is limited to MAXINT-1,
and that score has been repeatedly achieved.

The "NetHack's score is now meaningless" issue is a
separate problem from farming, NetHack scoring is
simply profoundly broken, to the point of being
meaningless, and band-aids that fix only one or two
of the problems aren't going to make the score any
more meaningful.

Scoring needs to be fixed, as a separate issue, but
the problem of _how_ to fix scoring is so difficult
even to analyze, that an acceptable fix may never
happen.

> why would farming need to exist? Who would go to
> the trouble of farming for no actual benefit?

Me, for one.

Pudding farming is a fun intellectual challenge, and
a fun exercise for practicing patience, other
rewards or no. Since I've played for almost twenty
years without ascending, I think I can safely say
that for me, the playing's the thing, not winning,
and so whether pudding farming helps me win is
entirely irrelevant. Nor can I be accuse of farming
"to make winning easier", since it doesn't, nor has
all that farming gotten me any close to ascension.

Quantum valeat.

